PROTOCOL="# V43 locked implementation protocol\n\nThis protocol implements the supplied V43_fast_slow_authority_design.md, preserved byte-for-byte as ORIGINAL_DESIGN.md. The roster is 16 fresh seeds 43101–43116 at total identity loads 64, 128, 256 and 512: 64 physical learning trajectories. Eight online policies share one base/SUPER/SLOTS state per trajectory. Offline SHUFFLED and oracles are read comparisons, not independent learning trajectories. No outcomes select these refinements.\n\nThe independent review below supplies the adopted operational resolutions. The specification's Q0–Q10 numbers and Outcome A formula remain unchanged. Load 512 is a stress cell; failed physical validity is reported explicitly. No seed or configuration is added in response to science.\n\n**Execution details.** Load means total identities: keys_per_wave=load//4, repeats=8, trace capacity=512, slot capacity=384. The inherited generator, raw stream semantics, encoder, temperature, base/fast/slow writes, admission, promotion and eviction remain unchanged. No FULL-HYBRID physical branch is needed. The historical READ-HYBRID zero-norm fallback is retained and counted; primary architectures use raw SUPER as their fast distribution. Engineering uses seeds 943001 and 943002 at both loads 64 and 256, disjoint from science. Smoke uses seed 943901, 16 identities and two repeats, and never enters inference.\n\nEvidence uses stable float64 log probabilities and is never clipped. Physical hashes include learned and fixed arrays, context, ordered containers, counters and future-influencing RNG state. Every byte scores all online policies before the common observation. Checkpoints preserve all physical state, virtual ledgers, event records, cursor and metrics. The default checkpoint block is eight complete 14-byte records, an execution setting that may change on resume. Verify atomic current/previous checkpoints, real SIGINT/SIGKILL resume equivalence, corruption and identity rejection, and writer exclusion. Workers are independent seed/load cells. Default concurrency is four, with one BLAS thread per worker.\n\n**Shuffle details.** Compute age quartile cutpoints over all route-G pre-event slot ages within seed/load using NumPy linear quantiles at .25, .5 and .75; assign with searchsorted(side='right'). Ties may leave empty bins. Cross age bins with retained-support and prior-G-use bins. Within size≥2 strata use a deterministic, outcome-independent derangement. Preserve permutation indices and bin assignments. Singleton weights retain their original values for full-G descriptions and are excluded from Q6. Count changed assignments and changed numerical weights separately. SHUFFLED accuracy and checkpoint recall cannot be recovered from saved true-byte probabilities and remain omitted.\n\n**Diagnostic details.** Fixed logistic, spline-logistic and gradient-boosting analyses leave one entire seed out across all loads. Their fits are post hoc analyses, never physical learner updates or qualification inputs. Completed folds are checkpointed. The diagnostic module exports its complete configuration and feature list. No event subsampling or parameter search is planned.\n\n**Output accounting.** Raw A/T/G authority events use compressed columnar NPZ per trajectory, with a combined table/index for analysis. Fast-only bytes retain aggregate counts and losses. Training presentations, online authority events, checkpoint probes and diagnostic fits are counted separately. Completed archives omit finished large physical checkpoints; partial archives retain unfinished ones. Hash manifests cover the outputs.\n\n# V43 independent design review\n\nReviewed the complete `V43_fast_slow_authority_design.md` and decoded V41 hybrid, memory, and stream implementations before V43 science. This review proposes implementation resolutions; the runner's locked protocol must identify which resolutions it adopts. The scientific roster remains seeds 43101–43116 × loads 64, 128, 256, 512, with every read policy sharing one physical trajectory. No outcome-driven tuning is justified.\n\n## Source facts that materially constrain implementation\n\n1. **Load means total identities.** The inherited four-wave generator takes `keys_per_wave=load//4`; preserve V41's eight acquisition presentations, noise/revision rows, RNG call order, and 512-trace/384-slot caps. Load 128 then reproduces the V41 workload configuration on fresh seeds.\n2. **The internal slow-write fallback is the base.** V41's SLOTS lookup receives `base_scores`. READ-HYBRID changes scored predictions only. Feeding SUPER or a mixture to lookup changes admission even if the update code is untouched.\n3. **Mature support is exactly two in the locked TRACE-CORR implementation.** Support is retained-anchor cardinality, not hits or distinct lifetime uses. Therefore the 3–4 and 5+ shuffle support bins will be empty by construction. Report this honestly; do not substitute access count to populate bins.\n4. **Native allocation IDs are already monotone.** `Memory.serial` is consumed by traces and slots, and mature slot dictionary keys are unique serial IDs. A reused packed-array position, if an engineering representation uses one, must never replace this UID.\n5. **No explicit revision-commit event exists.** All exact-anchor observations update the shared slot value with fixed smoothing. The physical learner neither recognizes evaluator revision labels nor emits a semantic-commit event. A concrete causal definition is needed: a revision commit is a change in the slot value's deterministic argmax across one physical exact-anchor update. Reset both local ledgers after that commit. Do not reset on every value update; that prevents evidence accumulation. Do not reset using stream revision/noise tags.\n6. **Exact historical READ fallback has a zero-score corner.** V41 uses SUPER scores when their norm exceeds 1e-9, otherwise base scores; SUPER itself is raw SUPER scores. Explicitly preserve that historical baseline or document that the V43 named baseline follows the spec's fast-everywhere table at this corner. Count differences. Physical reproduction concerns unchanged learning state in either case.\n\n## Recommended frozen operational resolutions\n\n### Causality and lifecycle\n\nClassify A/T/G/F using the one inherited nearest-candidate result: an exact mature anchor wins, then exact trace; a nonexact authoritative mature candidate is G; everything else is F. A tentative trace can win the nearest-candidate competition and block a less-similar mature slot. Searching mature slots separately would change the locked addressing rule.\n\n`E2` initialization means actual two-context trace promotion, including ordinary nontarget bytes and promotions occurring at an evaluator exposure other than 2. Before revealing the byte, capture the selected trace's full distribution and the SUPER distribution even when the deployed route is F. Once the unchanged learner actually promotes, initialize LOCAL-E2 with the frozen trace-versus-fast log ratio. Do not infer promotion from labels, scheduled exposure counts, or post-update values. If several transitions occur, apply evidence to the old generation, then removal/birth/reset in actual transition order.\n\nGLOBAL-BAYES accumulates every observed G event over the full trajectory. The specification does not reset its global ledger when one slot revises or evicts; preserve it. Both local ledgers reset to zero on a committed slot revision; evicted generations are removed. Retain historical event records for reporting, without making them deployable tombstones. A generation's prior similarity-use count is lifetime G uses since birth; a ledger reset does not silently reset this age/use covariate. Revision age is undefined until first revision, then elapsed physical bytes since the most recent commit.\n\nEvaluator probes read the *current* causal weights from existing ledgers. They do not update local/global evidence, counters, slot recency, RNG, or any learner buffer. First two aliases being evaluated at E1/E2 is evaluator bookkeeping only. Probe order must be immaterial. SHUFFLED is defined for saved online G events and has no automatically defined checkpoint-probe weight; do not fabricate SHUFFLED held-out scores. SHUFFLED's top1 online accuracy requires full G expert vectors or sufficient exact argmax geometry, not just true-byte probabilities. It is valid to report only its specified loss-based contrast if accuracy is unavailable.\n\nCompute specialist evidence from stable pre-update log probabilities. Do not floor/clamp probabilities in a way that clips the scientific evidence ledger. Stable logaddexp gives mixture loss even if a float64 probability underflows. Preserve the inherited output temperature. All features used for deployed prediction must predate the outcome; `true_byte`, expert correctness, and outcome losses enter only scoring, evidence updates, and offline diagnostics.\n\n### Shuffled control\n\nUse LOCAL-BAYES-E2 weights as the unqualified word LOCAL in SHUFFLED-ALPHA. Fix a definition of age quartiles before science. A defensible choice is full-trajectory G-event age quantiles within each seed/load, computed using a documented quantile interpolation and deterministic boundary rule; ties may create fewer than four nonempty bins. These cut points are offline and cannot enter deployed predictions. Alternatively ranked quartiles with event-index tie-breaking are reproducible, but tie splitting must be explicit.\n\nCross the age bin with exact support bins {2,3–4,5+} and *pre-event* lifetime G-use bins {0–1,2–3,4+}. Use an outcome-independent deterministic derangement or nonzero cyclic shift within every stratum of size at least 2. Singleton weights remain unchanged for descriptive whole-policy totals but are excluded from the decisive specificity comparison. Report both changed event assignments and changed numerical weights: saturation or equal weights can make the latter zero even under a perfect derangement. Do not retune strata to manufacture 80% coverage.\n\nMultiset identity establishes exact authority-mass preservation; compare sums in an order-independent canonical order or with `math.fsum`, since naive different-order floating-point summation can differ in its last bit. Save permutation indices and bin assignments. Q6 uses LOCAL and SHUFFLED on exactly the same permutable-event subset, normalized by that subset's G count. Full-G policy summaries remain separately available. Require 80% permutable coverage in every load 256 seed as a conservative concrete interpretation of the coverage requirement.\n\n### Endpoint/gate denominators\n\nThe scientific unit is the seed throughout. Compute each seed/load endpoint first, then equally weight the 16 seed values. Event-pooled descriptive totals are useful but must not replace paired inference.\n\n* **Durable old held-out accuracy:** inherit V41 `A_after_D_heldout`, the untouched-A identities at alias2 after D. Also retain the stricter same-identity E1-and-all-delays endpoint as secondary; do not substitute it after seeing results.\n* **Q0 acquisition:** assess the unchanged physical SLOTS path on all intended current-wave identities at learned aliases0/1 at each after_A/B/C/D checkpoint. Do not condition the denominator on surviving slots or correct acquisition. A cell is acquisition-valid only if every checkpoint reaches 90%; report all checkpoint fractions. Any invalid 128/256 cell prevents the complete preregistered 16-seed qualification; an observed-valid subset may be descriptive but cannot be presented as the full experiment. Load 512 is stress-descriptive when its substrate is invalid.\n* **Q1:** both 128 and 256 must have at least 500 G events in every seed; at each load the seed-equal average `(hard loss − event oracle loss)/nG` must be at least0.20. Do not let one high-headroom load rescue the other.\n* **Q2:** compute each seed/load A-event mean difference first. Across the 32 values at 128/256 require mean≤0 and maximum≤0.05. Empty anchor samples are unavailable, never zero/passing. This avoids a good seed/load masking a bad one.\n* **Q3:** equal-seed comparisons at each primary load 128/256; SILENT-HARD whole-bpb minus READ≤0, E1 difference≥−0.02, and exactly identical physical consolidation counts. Report other loads separately.\n* **Q4/Q5/Q6:** retain the numerical thresholds and pointwise paired 95% bounds exactly as written; Q6 uses only permutable G events. Do not silently replace these bounds by event bootstrap intervals.\n* **Q7:** a simpler policy matches if, separately at both 128 and 256, simple−LOCAL≤0.01 whole bpb, simple−LOCAL≤0.02 G bpb, and simple−LOCAL≥−0.02 held-out accuracy. This is one-sided practical matching: a clearly superior simple policy also counts. Requiring absolute differences would absurdly disqualify a better simple policy. Report both candidates; if both match, prefer FIXED-50 because it has no learned arbitration state. The spec supplies no confidence-interval gate for Q7, so present point estimates and uncertainty without adding a new test.\n* **Q8:** compute each seed's capture fraction then equal-seed average; separately report ratio-of-summed-gains and denominators. Zero/negligible headroom is undefined and cannot pass by setting capture to 0 or 1. Q1 gives the meaningful-headroom prerequisite. Capture can exceed1 because a probability mixture may beat the event oracle that chooses only between fixed experts; do not clip it.\n* **Q9:** use the equal-seed mean whole bpb gap at 256≤0.05 and Q5 as specified.\n* **Q10:** the word “materially” has no number. A consistent explicit operationalization is no positive LOCAL−HARD whole bpb difference at either128 or256, and the change in LOCAL−HARD durable accuracy from 128 to 256≥−0.02. This reuses the existing 2 pp margin. Report confidence intervals on the load interaction. The original Outcome A formula omits Q10; do not silently rewrite that formula. Report mechanism qualification and scaling status distinctly.\n\n### Statistical family and scaling analysis\n\nUse paired Student-t intervals over 16 seed differences (15 degrees of freedom), alongside seed tables and exact sign-flip sensitivity where useful. Predefine the decisive load 256 family of four contrasts: LOCAL−HARD whole bpb, LOCAL−GLOBAL whole bpb, LOCAL−FIXED whole bpb, and LOCAL−SHUFFLED permutable-G bpb. Holm-adjust these four two-sided p-values if reporting inferential p-values. The SUPER comparison is an engineering-gap contrast, not a fifth mechanistic test. Other endpoints and loads are secondary with explicitly labeled within-load families or descriptive intervals; claiming one omnibus adjusted family after testing4 contrasts × many endpoints is inappropriate. Qualification still uses the spec's effect thresholds and stated 95% bounds, with adjusted p-values reported alongside rather than inventing new gates.\n\nFor scaling, use seed-blocked load-specific means and paired-difference regressions on log2(load), with seed clustering; preserve seed grouping across all four loads. Report policy×load interactions from this repeated-measures structure. Held-out L50 is estimable only if observed valid loads actually bracket 50% and the fitted curve supports a crossing; otherwise state not identified in the tested range rather than extrapolate. Dominance ordering is conditional on measured endpoints/loads and can be summarized with seed bootstrap over complete seed blocks, not by treating 64 cells or millions of events as independent.\n\n### Exploratory predictability\n\nLeave one entire seed out, across all its loads, for each fold. Fit all imputation, scaling, transforms, calibration, and any tuning only on training seeds. Do not use slotUID/keyID, the byte outcome, correctness, losses, post-outcome evidence, or eventwise future rank/quantiles as predictive covariates. Physical age, current evidence, expert entropy/margin/agreement/divergence, causal similarities, and prior-use counts are appropriate. The offline diagnostic estimates predictability conditional on G routing; it is not a validated deployable policy and cannot repair failed Q4/Q5/Q6 gates. Report class prevalence and simple constant/logistic baselines along with AUC, logloss, calibration, and headroom capture.\n\n## Verification priorities\n\nEngineering seeds must be disjoint from43101–43116; the literal safest reading of “at least two ... seeds at loads64and 256” is two seeds × both loads. Reproduce the base, SUPER, and SLOTS state against unchanged V41 code on identical generated rows, including physical RNG/counters and terminal probes. Exclude the irrelevant FULL-HYBRID branch from physical-state matching. Hashing must include all mutable future-influencing arrays, dictionary insertion order, allocation counters and generators; a purported complete hash that omits scratch buffers requires proof they are both unlearned and behaviorally inert.\n\nCheck interruption/resume against uninterrupted output equality with checkpointed evaluator state, evidence ledgers, event tables, stream cursor and RNG. Probe purity must include virtual ledgers as well as physical state. Generation reuse and revision-reset fixtures must deliberately put nonzero evidence in the retiring/reset ledger. Full policy scorer invariance must be checked separately from the common physical update. Final outputs should explicitly distinguish64 physical trajectories, counterfactual scoring policies, physical byte events, and evaluator-only reads.\n\n## Interpretation limit\n\nA success would support causal arbitration on the inherited synthetic address geometry, not establish natural-language persistent learning, biological equivalence, optimal forgetting, or independent policy training replicates. E2 seeding is selected on a successful promotion event by design; LOCAL-E2 versus LOCAL-0 helps describe that initialization contribution, but cannot make the selected seed statistic independent corroboration. The shuffled control tests event/object alignment relative to its chosen marginal-preserving strata, not a universal theorem that object-local evidence is necessary.\n\n\n**Complete-state hashing execution refinement.** To avoid repeatedly scanning approximately 11 MB of unchanged buffers for every byte, the engine uses a complete Merkle representation of the physical state. Arrays are read-only during prediction; all ordered containers, counters, RNG and metadata are traversed. After the single authorized learner update, the changed base bank and fast rows refresh their leaves; new slow-memory array leaves are hashed directly. The cached root is checked against a complete uncached recomputation after every 14-byte record, in engineering and science. Full canonical component fingerprints are also checked at workload checkpoints. This changes verification cost only. Independent native replay must reproduce every physical component, event count and terminal prediction before science. Hash caches are execution bookkeeping, are not physical memory, and cannot enter a prediction or update.\n\nParent death is checked by each worker at checkpoint boundaries. A killed parent therefore costs at most the currently unfinished block before orphaned workers save and stop; a replacement worker waits for the per-cell writer lock. Top-level concurrent runners are rejected. Engineering replays also save both compared states every eight records. Diagnostic interruption is honored before and after each complete fitted fold. The pause-after-checkpoints option is a per-cell engineering aid, not a scientific stopping rule.\n"
ORIGINAL_PROTOCOL="# V43 — Fast–Slow Authority\n## When may mature similarity-based object memory override a fast bounded memory?\n\n**Status:** preregistration / implementation specification only.\n\n**Primary scientific question**\n\n\\[\n\x08oxed{\n\text{When both fast superposed memory and mature explicit object memory have an answer,\nwhich one should control prediction?}\n}\n\\]\n\n**Primary candidate:** `LOCAL-BAYES-E2`  \n**Primary specificity control:** `SHUFFLED-ALPHA`  \n**Simpler controls:** `FIXED-50`, `GLOBAL-BAYES`  \n**Physical learner:** V41 `SLOTS/READ-HYBRID` learning trajectory, frozen as the common substrate  \n**Primary structural change from V42:** probationary traces are silent for prediction  \n**Mature exact anchors:** hard slow authority  \n**Only mature supported-similarity reads are arbitrated**\n\n**Scientific panel:** 16 fresh seeds × loads {64, 128, 256, 512} = 64 physical trajectories.  \nAll read policies are scored on the same physical trajectory for each seed/load.\n\nNo parameter sweep. No new encoder. No new write rule. No new admission rule. No utility eviction. No phase-normalization branch.\n\n---\n\n# 1. Motivation\n\nV42 decomposed the remaining READ-HYBRID penalty approximately as\n\n\\[\nL_{\nm READ}-L_{\nm SUPER}\n\x07pprox\n+0.0576_{\nm probationary\\ exact}\n+\n0.0619_{\nm supported\\ similarity}\n-\n0.0129_{\nm mature\\ exact}\n\\quad{\nm bpb}.\n\\]\n\nThe implications are:\n\n1. mature exact consolidated anchors are mildly beneficial;\n2. hard probationary-trace authority is costly;\n3. supported mature-slot similarity is necessary for durable held-out alias recall but costly on ordinary prediction;\n4. the fast superposed layer already supplies strong one-shot behavior.\n\nV43 therefore freezes the memory architecture and manipulates only mature similarity authority.\n\nProposed hierarchy:\n\n\\[\n\x08oxed{\n\x08egin{array}{c}\n\text{shared predictive base}\\\n\\downarrow\\\n\text{fast bounded superposed memory}\\\n\\downarrow\\\n\text{silent probationary traces}\\\n\\downarrow\\\n\text{mature explicit object slots}\n\\end{array}}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n# 2. Non-negotiable architectural firewall\n\nEvery seed/load has exactly one physical learner trajectory.\n\nThe physical learner contains:\n\n- shared base;\n- fast superposed store;\n- slow explicit trace/slot learner;\n- unchanged admission, consolidation, revision, eviction, and capacity machinery.\n\nRead policy must never affect learning:\n\n\\[\n\x08oxed{\n\text{read policy}\n\not\nightarrow\n\text{base write, fast write, trace creation, slot promotion, revision, eviction}.\n}\n\\]\n\nThe slow learner must use exactly the same internal fallback and admission logic as the locked V41 `SLOTS/READ-HYBRID` shared learning path.\n\n**The scored fast/slow mixture is never fed back into the physical learner.**\n\nAll V43 policies are counterfactual readouts over identical physical state.\n\nAny policy-specific physical-state divergence voids the experiment.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Exact route taxonomy\n\nEvery event is classified before the true byte is observed into exactly one route.\n\n## A — mature exact anchor\n\nExact context is one of a mature slot's retained anchors.\n\nPrimary architecture:\n\n\\[\np=p_S.\n\\]\n\nNo V43 authority manipulation.\n\n## T — probationary exact trace\n\nExact context exists only in the probationary trace tier.\n\nPrimary architecture:\n\n\\[\np=p_F.\n\\]\n\nTrace state remains available for post-outcome corroboration/consolidation but is silent for prediction.\n\nHistorical `READ-HYBRID` may hard-read it as a baseline.\n\n## G — mature supported similarity\n\nNo exact mature anchor, but a mature slot is a supported similarity candidate under the locked addressing rule.\n\nThis is the **only** route V43 manipulates.\n\nAvailable experts:\n\n\\[\np_F,\\qquad p_S.\n\\]\n\n## F — fast fallback\n\nNo mature exact anchor and no supported mature similarity route.\n\n\\[\np=p_F.\n\\]\n\nRoute classification must be deterministic and policy-independent.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Fast and slow experts\n\n`p_F` is the full pre-update distribution of the V41 SUPER fast tier.\n\nIt is not the base-only distribution.\n\nThe base distribution `p_B` is logged only for diagnostics.\n\nFor route G, `p_S` is the mature slot's ordinary pre-update probability distribution.\n\nFor route A, `p_S` is the exact mature-anchor prediction.\n\nFor route T, a counterfactual `p_T` may be logged but is not deployed by the proposed architecture.\n\nAll distributions come from the same physical pre-update state.\n\n---\n\n# 5. Specialist evidence\n\nFor each mature slot generation \\(j\\), maintain a virtual evidence ledger\n\n\\[\nE_j(t)\n=\n\\sum_{\tau<t,\\;\tau\\in G_j}\n\\log_2\n\x0crac{p_{S,j,\tau}(y_\tau)}\n     {p_{F,\tau}(y_\tau)}.\n\\]\n\nInclude only prior route-G events for that slot generation.\n\nExclude:\n\n- mature exact anchors;\n- probationary trace events;\n- unsupported nearest candidates;\n- evaluator probes;\n- events after eviction;\n- events from a previous generation of a reused slot index.\n\nInterpretation:\n\n\\[\nE_j>0\n\\]\n\nmeans slow similarity has historically outpredicted the fast tier for this object.\n\nConvert evidence to authority:\n\n\\[\n\x08oxed{\nw_j\n=\n\x0crac{2^{E_j}}{1+2^{E_j}}\n=\n\\sigma(E_j\\ln2).\n}\n\\]\n\nOn route G:\n\n\\[\n\x08oxed{\np=w_jp_S+(1-w_j)p_F.\n}\n\\]\n\nUse a numerically stable logistic implementation. Store `E_j` in float64. Do not clip the scientific ledger; only protect numerical evaluation of the logistic.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Evidence update order\n\nFor each event:\n\n1. construct current context;\n2. hash complete physical state;\n3. compute `p_B` and `p_F`;\n4. classify route A/T/G/F;\n5. compute `p_S` or `p_T` as applicable;\n6. score all V43 read policies;\n7. record all pre-outcome features;\n8. reveal `y`;\n9. record policy losses;\n10. update virtual evidence ledgers;\n11. execute one common physical learner update;\n12. process promotion/revision/eviction ledger lifecycle;\n13. verify no policy changed physical state.\n\nNo policy may inspect `y` before step 8.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Slot-generation lifecycle\n\nNever key evidence by a reusable array index.\n\nEach mature memory needs a monotone unique `slot_uid` / `generation_uid`.\n\n## Consolidation\n\nTwo candidate initializations:\n\n### LOCAL-BAYES-0\n\n\\[\nE_j=0.\n\\]\n\n### LOCAL-BAYES-E2\n\nAt E2 promotion:\n\n\\[\n\x08oxed{\nE_j^{(0)}\n=\n\\log_2\n\x0crac{p_T(y_{E2})}\n     {p_F(y_{E2})}.\n}\n\\]\n\n`p_T` and `p_F` must both be computed before the E2 outcome and before promotion.\n\nThis statistic may not alter whether promotion occurs.\n\n## Revision\n\nWhen a slot-wide semantic revision commits:\n\n\\[\nE_j\\leftarrow0.\n\\]\n\n## Eviction\n\nDestroy the generation ledger.\n\nNo tombstone.\n\n## Re-consolidation\n\nAllocate a fresh generation and fresh ledger.\n\nNo evidence inheritance.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Read policies\n\nAll policies share the same physical trajectory.\n\n## SUPER\n\nFast everywhere.\n\n## READ-HYBRID\n\nHistorical baseline:\n- A: slow;\n- T: trace;\n- G: slow;\n- F: fast.\n\n## SILENT-HARD\n\nPrimary structural baseline:\n- A: slow;\n- T: fast;\n- G: hard slow;\n- F: fast.\n\n## ANCHOR-ONLY\n\n- A: slow;\n- T: fast;\n- G: fast;\n- F: fast.\n\n## FIXED-50\n\nOn G:\n\n\\[\np=.5p_S+.5p_F.\n\\]\n\nElse use the primary architecture.\n\n## GLOBAL-BAYES\n\nMaintain\n\n\\[\nE_G\n=\n\\sum_{\tau<t,\tau\\in G}\n\\log_2\x0crac{p_S(y_\tau)}{p_F(y_\tau)}\n\\]\n\nand use\n\n\\[\nw_G=\\sigma(E_G\\ln2).\n\\]\n\n## LOCAL-BAYES-0\n\nPer-slot evidence initialized at zero.\n\n## LOCAL-BAYES-E2\n\nPer-slot evidence seeded from the E2 trace-vs-fast log likelihood ratio.\n\n**Primary V43 candidate.**\n\nIf the exact pre-E2 quantities cannot be obtained without altering the physical learner, drop this arm before science. Do not approximate it post hoc.\n\n## SHUFFLED-ALPHA\n\nPrimary nondeployable specificity control, computed offline from the saved authority-event table.\n\nTake the actual pre-outcome LOCAL authority weights \\(w_t\\) on route G.\n\nWithin each seed × load, stratify by:\n\n- support: `2`, `3–4`, `5+`;\n- slot-age quartile;\n- prior similarity-use count: `0–1`, `2–3`, `4+`.\n\nWithin each permutable stratum, deterministically permute the LOCAL weights across events:\n\n\\[\np_t=w_{\\pi(t)}p_{S,t}+(1-w_{\\pi(t)})p_{F,t}.\n\\]\n\nThis must preserve exactly within each permutable stratum:\n\n- authority-weight multiset;\n- total authority mass;\n- number of events;\n- fast and slow predictions;\n- physical trajectory.\n\nIt destroys the alignment between earned authority and the object/event that earned it.\n\nSingleton strata are reported and excluded from the decisive shuffled contrast.\n\nAt least 80% of route-G events used in the specificity test must lie in permutable strata.\n\n## EVENT-ORACLE\n\nDiagnostic only:\n\n\\[\n\\ell_O(t)=\\min(\\ell_F(t),\\ell_S(t)).\n\\]\n\n## SLOT-ORACLE\n\nDiagnostic only: for each slot generation, retrospectively select whichever fixed expert, FAST or SLOW, had lower cumulative route-G log loss.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Oracle headroom\n\nFor route-G events:\n\n\\[\nL_H=\\sum\\ell_S\n\\]\n\nunder hard similarity authority, and\n\n\\[\nL_O=\\sum\\min(\\ell_S,\\ell_F).\n\\]\n\nAvailable headroom:\n\n\\[\n\x08oxed{H=L_H-L_O.}\n\\]\n\nFor policy \\(m\\):\n\n\\[\n\x08oxed{\nC_m\n=\n\x0crac{L_H-L_m}{L_H-L_O}.\n}\n\\]\n\nThis is the fraction of theoretically available arbitration gain captured.\n\nIf oracle headroom is negligible, do not interpret tiny policy differences as a mechanism discovery.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Authority-event instrumentation\n\nFor every A/T/G event, record compact pre-outcome features:\n\n```text\nseed\nload\nevent_index\nphysical_time\nroute\nslot_uid\ngeneration_uid\nsupport\nslot_age\ntime_since_last_use\nprior_similarity_use_count\nsimilarity_top1\nsimilarity_top2\nsimilarity_margin\nfast_top1\nslow_top1\nfast_slow_agree\nfast_entropy\nslow_entropy\nfast_margin\nslow_margin\njs_divergence\nlocal_E_before\nlocal_w_before\nrevision_age\nwas_revised\n```\n\nAfter `y` is revealed, append:\n\n```text\ntrue_byte\npB_true\npF_true\npS_true\nslow_minus_fast_loss\n```\n\nDo not dump every ordinary fast-only byte event.\n\nTop-1 accuracy for preregistered policies should be accumulated online. Full 256-way distributions need not be written to disk unless needed for engineering audit.\n\nRecommended storage: Parquet or NPZ.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Exploratory predictability diagnostic\n\nOn route G define\n\n\\[\nZ_t=\\mathbf 1\\{\\ell_S(t)<\\ell_F(t)\\}.\n\\]\n\nUsing only pre-outcome features, fit nondeployable diagnostics:\n\n1. logistic regression;\n2. spline/GAM if available;\n3. gradient boosting as a flexible ceiling.\n\nValidation must be **leave-one-seed-out**, never random event splitting.\n\nReport:\n\n- ROC-AUC;\n- log loss;\n- calibration;\n- fraction of EVENT-ORACLE headroom captured.\n\nThis does not determine qualification.\n\nIts purpose is to answer whether the fast-vs-slow mistake is predictably identifiable from causal state.\n\n---\n\n# 12. Engineering invariants\n\nRun at least two non-science engineering seeds at loads 64 and 256.\n\n## E0 — physical reproduction\n\nWith arbitration disabled, reproduce the locked V41/V42 physical trajectory:\n\n- base hashes;\n- fast-store hashes;\n- slow-memory hashes;\n- promotion/revision/eviction counts;\n- terminal physical probes.\n\nAny unexplained mismatch stops V43.\n\n## E1 — policy-state firewall\n\nScoring all policies must leave the physical hash unchanged.\n\nPolicies may maintain only virtual arbitration ledgers.\n\n## E2 — complete physical hashing\n\nHash must include:\n\n- all learned arrays;\n- traces/slots;\n- allocation counters;\n- slot-generation counters;\n- RNG state that can influence future learning;\n- admission/eviction counters.\n\nThis explicitly prevents the earlier bug where evaluator probes advanced hidden RNG/buffer state absent from the hash.\n\n## E3 — probe purity\n\nEvaluator probes may not alter:\n\n- physical state;\n- virtual ledgers;\n- RNG positions used by learning.\n\n## E4 — route exclusivity\n\nEvery event maps to exactly one of A/T/G/F.\n\nCounts must sum to total events.\n\nExact mature anchors may not also count as G.\n\n## E5 — causality\n\nAssert that:\n\n- all policy predictions finalize before `observe(y)`;\n- ledger updates occur after `y`;\n- E2 seed uses pre-E2 distributions;\n- no future metadata enters current prediction.\n\n## E6 — generation safety\n\nEngineering fixture:\n\n- birth;\n- eviction;\n- slot-index reuse;\n- re-consolidation.\n\nVerify zero evidence inheritance.\n\n## E7 — revision reset\n\nEngineering fixture with positive evidence followed by committed revision.\n\nVerify exact reset to zero.\n\n## E8 — shuffled exactness\n\nFor each permutable stratum:\n\n- identical authority-weight multiset before/after permutation;\n- identical total authority mass;\n- substantial reassignment;\n- no physical-state access beyond saved features.\n\n---\n\n# 13. Scientific panel\n\nFresh seeds:\n\n```text\n43101–43116\n```\n\nLoads:\n\n\\[\n64,\\;128,\\;256,\\;512.\n\\]\n\nTotal physical trajectories:\n\n\\[\n16\times4=64.\n\\]\n\nEvery trajectory scores every read policy.\n\nLoad 512 is a stress cell. If the underlying physical learner itself fails acquisition there, mark it `physical_capacity_invalid`; do not use it to judge arbitration.\n\nNo adaptive seed addition based on science outcomes.\n\n---\n\n# 14. Primary endpoints\n\n1. whole-stream bpb;\n2. route-G bpb;\n3. durable old held-out accuracy;\n4. oracle-headroom capture \\(C_m\\).\n\nSecondary:\n\n- target/nontarget bpb;\n- anchor bpb vs fast;\n- trace bpb vs fast;\n- E1/E2 held-out accuracy;\n- revision exact/known/held-out;\n- route counts;\n- authority mass;\n- fast/slow agreement;\n- evidence distributions;\n- SLOT-ORACLE loss.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Statistical analysis\n\nThe independent scientific unit is the seed.\n\nAuthority events are not independent replicates.\n\n## Planned paired contrasts\n\nAt each load:\n\n1. LOCAL-E2 − SILENT-HARD\n2. LOCAL-E2 − FIXED-50\n3. LOCAL-E2 − GLOBAL-BAYES\n4. LOCAL-E2 − SHUFFLED-ALPHA\n5. LOCAL-E2 − SUPER\n\nUse paired seed-level effects and intervals.\n\n## Hierarchical load analysis\n\nFit seed-blocked/hierarchical models across valid loads for:\n\n- whole bpb;\n- G-route bpb;\n- durable held-out success.\n\nUse \\(\\log_2(\text{load})\\) as the ordered pressure axis.\n\nEstimate:\n\n- load-specific means;\n- policy × load interaction;\n- held-out \\(L_{50}\\) where identifiable;\n- probability/order of policy dominance over the observed load range.\n\n## Multiplicity\n\nThe decisive mechanistic family is:\n\n- LOCAL vs SILENT-HARD;\n- LOCAL vs GLOBAL;\n- LOCAL vs FIXED-50;\n- LOCAL vs SHUFFLED.\n\nIf frequentist p-values are reported, use Holm adjustment across these four planned contrasts.\n\nEffect sizes and intervals remain primary.\n\n---\n\n# 16. Qualification gates\n\n## Q0 — physical validity\n\nE0–E8 pass.\n\nEvery science cell used in inference has:\n\n- no physical-state divergence;\n- finite probabilities/losses;\n- physical learner acquisition ≥90% on intended current mature memories.\n\n## Q1 — arbitration headroom\n\nAt loads 128 and 256:\n\n- at least 500 G-route events per seed;\n- hard-G loss exceeds EVENT-ORACLE by ≥0.20 bits/G-event on average.\n\nOtherwise arbitration is not a meaningful bottleneck.\n\n## Q2 — mature anchors remain safe\n\nAcross 128 and 256:\n\n\\[\n\\ell_A^{slow}-\\ell_A^{fast}\\le0\n\\]\n\non average, with no seed mean disadvantage worse than +0.05 bits/A-event.\n\nIf this fails, unconditional anchor authority must be reopened.\n\n## Q3 — silent traces are viable\n\nRelative to READ-HYBRID, SILENT-HARD must:\n\n- improve or match whole bpb;\n- preserve E1 held-out within 2 pp;\n- preserve physical consolidation counts exactly.\n\n## Q4 — primary prediction gain\n\nAt load 256:\n\n\\[\n\text{bpb}_{LOCAL-E2}\n-\n\text{bpb}_{SILENT-HARD}\n\\le-0.03\n\\]\n\nwith paired 95% upper bound below zero.\n\n## Q5 — durable alias noninferiority\n\nAt load 256:\n\n\\[\n\text{heldout}_{LOCAL-E2}\n\\ge\n\text{heldout}_{SILENT-HARD}-0.02.\n\\]\n\nPaired lower bound for LOCAL − SILENT-HARD must exceed −0.05.\n\n## Q6 — specificity veto\n\nAt load 256 on route G:\n\n\\[\n\text{bpb}_{LOCAL-E2}\n-\n\text{bpb}_{SHUFFLED-ALPHA}\n\\le-0.05\n\\]\n\nwith paired 95% upper bound below zero.\n\nAt least 80% of compared G events must belong to permutable strata.\n\nIf Q6 fails, object/event-specific learned authority is not established.\n\n## Q7 — complexity must earn itself\n\nIf FIXED-50 or GLOBAL-BAYES is within all of:\n\n- 0.01 whole bpb;\n- 0.02 G-route bpb;\n- 2 pp durable held-out accuracy\n\nof LOCAL-E2 across loads 128 and 256, prefer the simpler policy.\n\n## Q8 — oracle capture\n\nAt load 256:\n\n\\[\nC_{LOCAL-E2}\\ge0.50.\n\\]\n\n## Q9 — end-to-end target\n\nAt load 256:\n\n\\[\n\text{whole bpb}_{LOCAL-E2}\n\\le\n\text{whole bpb}_{SUPER}+0.05\n\\]\n\nwhile Q5 holds.\n\nIf Q4/Q6/Q8 pass but Q9 fails, the mechanism is supported but the architecture gap remains.\n\n## Q10 — scaling stability\n\nFrom load 128 to 256:\n\n- LOCAL advantage over SILENT-HARD must not reverse sign;\n- durable held-out degradation must not materially exceed SILENT-HARD.\n\nLoad 512 remains descriptive unless the physical substrate stays valid.\n\n---\n\n# 17. Decision logic\n\n## Outcome A — local specialist arbitration established\n\nQ0–Q6 and Q8 pass, LOCAL beats SHUFFLED, and no simpler rule matches under Q7.\n\nConclusion:\n\n> mature similarity authority is genuinely object/event specific and can be earned from the slot's own past predictive advantage over fast memory.\n\n## Outcome B — global arbitration is enough\n\nGLOBAL matches LOCAL.\n\nUse one global scalar.\n\n## Outcome C — fixed mixture is enough\n\nFIXED-50 matches adaptive policies.\n\nUse FIXED-50.\n\n## Outcome D — similarity should remain silent\n\nANCHOR-ONLY/SUPER dominates and no adaptive policy preserves durable held-out transfer economically.\n\nRevisit identity/addressing rather than adding more gates.\n\n## Outcome E — LOCAL looks best but fails shuffled specificity\n\nAdaptive authority magnitude helps, but correct object/event assignment is not established.\n\nDo not carry local evidence forward.\n\n## Outcome F — little oracle headroom\n\nQ1 fails.\n\nStop read-policy search.\n\n---\n\n# 18. Forbidden changes\n\nV43 must not modify:\n\n- base architecture;\n- superposed write rule;\n- slow write rule;\n- trace admission;\n- two-context consolidation;\n- trace/slot capacities;\n- revision;\n- eviction;\n- lag representation;\n- similarity threshold;\n- output temperature;\n- stream semantics.\n\nDo not add:\n\n- PBF-vs-base authority;\n- phase normalization;\n- new plasticity;\n- replay;\n- learned router;\n- utility eviction;\n- fast-memory unloading;\n- revision-confidence logic.\n\n---\n\n# 19. Required outputs\n\n```text\nSUMMARY.md\nREPORT.json\nMANIFEST.json\nPROTOCOL.md\nTERMINAL.csv\nLOAD_CURVES.csv\nROUTE_SUMMARY.csv\nAUTHORITY_EVENTS.parquet   # or .npz\nAUTHORITY_BY_SUPPORT.csv\nAUTHORITY_BY_AGE.csv\nPOLICY_CONTRASTS.csv\nORACLE_HEADROOM.csv\nSLOT_ORACLE.csv\nSHUFFLED_ALPHA_AUDIT.json\nSTATE_HASH_AUDIT.json\nREVISION_LEDGER_AUDIT.json\n```\n\nOptional:\n\n```text\nPREDICTABILITY_DIAGNOSTIC.csv\nPREDICTABILITY_FEATURES.csv\n```\n\nDo not dump full ordinary per-byte logs.\n\n---\n\n# 20. Runner contract\n\nOne self-contained executable file.\n\nSuggested interface:\n\n```bash\npython3 elm_v43_fast_slow_authority.py --self-test\npython3 elm_v43_fast_slow_authority.py --engineering\npython3 elm_v43_fast_slow_authority.py --out-dir v43_results\n```\n\nOne seed/load trajectory must score all policies in one pass.\n\nMinimal pseudocode:\n\n```python\nfor event in stream:\n    physical_hash_before = physical_state_hash()\n\n    pB = base.predict(context)\n    pF = fast.predict(context)\n\n    route = slow.classify_route(context)      # A/T/G/F\n    pS, pT, slot_uid = slow.counterfactual_distributions(context, route)\n\n    predictions = score_all_read_policies(\n        route=route,\n        pF=pF,\n        pS=pS,\n        pT=pT,\n        virtual_ledgers=ledgers,\n        slot_uid=slot_uid,\n    )\n\n    assert physical_state_hash() == physical_hash_before\n\n    y = event.next_byte\n\n    record_losses(predictions, y)\n    update_virtual_ledgers_after_outcome(route, slot_uid, pS, pF, y)\n\n    transition = physical_learner.observe(\n        context=context,\n        y=y,\n        internal_fallback=LOCKED_V41_FALLBACK,\n    )\n\n    apply_ledger_lifecycle(\n        transition=transition,\n        pre_event_pT=pT,\n        pre_event_pF=pF,\n        y=y,\n    )\n\n    assert no_policy_specific_physical_state()\n```\n\n`LOCKED_V41_FALLBACK` must be the exact value/path used by the shared V41 SLOTS/READ-HYBRID physical learner. Do not infer or replace it from prose.\n\n---\n\n# 21. Interpretation boundary\n\nA successful V43 would establish only:\n\n\\[\n\x08oxed{\n\text{fast distributed memory and slow durable object memory can coexist with a causal,\nlow-state arbitration rule that preserves durable alias recall while recovering much of\nthe fast tier's prediction quality.}\n}\n\\]\n\nIt would not establish:\n\n- optimal forgetting;\n- natural-language persistent learning;\n- noise-vs-revision discrimination;\n- biological equivalence;\n- universal optimality of Bayesian specialist arbitration.\n\nOnly after V43 should the project return to:\n\n1. marginal-utility survival under true scarcity;\n2. fast-memory unloading after consolidation;\n3. noise versus genuine revision;\n4. real byte-corpus validation.\n"
